### references/channel-setup.md  [docs]
+ # Channel Setup Guide
+ Detailed credential setup instructions for each supported messaging channel.
+ ## Telegram
+ 1. Open Telegram and search for **@BotFather**
+ 2. Send `/newbot` and follow the prompts to name your bot
+ 3. BotFather will give you a **Bot Token** (format: `1234567890:ABCdefGHI...`)
+ 4. Paste that token here
+ Required config field: `botToken`
+ ## Discord
+ 1. Go to [Discord Developer Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications)
+ 2. Click **New Application** → name it → go to **Bot** tab
+ 3. Click **Reset Token** and copy the token
+ 4. Under **Privileged Gateway Intents**, enable **Message Content Intent**
+ 5. Paste the token here
+ Required config field: `token`
+ ## Slack
+ 1. Go to [Slack API](https://api.slack.com/apps) → **Create New App**
+ 2. Enable **Socket Mode** → copy the **App-Level Token**
+ 3. Go to **OAuth & Permissions** → install to workspace → copy the **Bot User OAuth Token**
+ 4. Paste both tokens here
+ Required config fields: `appToken`, `botToken`
+ ## Feishu / Lark
+ 1. 打开 [飞书开放平台](https://open.feishu.cn/) → 创建企业自建应用
+ 2. 在 **凭证与基本信息** 页面找到 App ID 和 App Secret
+ 3. 在 **机器人** 功能页启用机器人能力
+ 4. 把 App ID 和 App Secret 发给我
+ For **Lark** (international): same steps at [Lark Developer](https://open.larksuite.com/). Add `"domain": "lark"` to the account entry.
+ Required config fields: `appId`, `appSecret`
+ ## WhatsApp
+ WhatsApp uses QR code login — no manual credentials needed:
+ ```bash
+ ```bash
+ openclaw channels login --channel whatsapp --account {name}
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ Scan the QR code with your WhatsApp app.
+ ## Signal
+ Signal uses QR code login — no manual credentials needed:
+ openclaw channels login --channel signal --account {name}
+ Scan the QR code with your Signal app (Settings → Linked Devices).
+ ## Google Chat
+ 1. Go to [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/) → create/select a project
+ 2. Enable the **Google Chat API**
+ 3. Create a **Service Account** → download the JSON key file
+ 4. Provide the path to the JSON file on this server
+ Required config field: `serviceAccountPath`
+ ## Channel Config Reference
+ | Channel | Config Path | Required |
+ |---------|------------|----------|
+ | Telegram | `channels.telegram.accounts.{name}` | `botToken` |
+ | Discord | `channels.discord.accounts.{name}` | `token` |
+ | Slack | `channels.slack.accounts.{name}` | `mode: "socket"`, `appToken`, `botToken` |
+ | Feishu | `channels.feishu.accounts.{name}` | `appId`, `appSecret` |
+ | WhatsApp | `channels.whatsapp.accounts.{name}` | QR scan via CLI |
+ | Signal | `channels.signal.accounts.{name}` | QR scan via CLI |
+ | Google Chat | `channels.googlechat.accounts.{name}` | `serviceAccountPath` |
+ ## Binding Format (all channels)
+ ```json
+ {
+   "agentId": "{name}-agent",
+   "match": {
+     "channel": "{channel}",
+     "accountId": "{name}"
+   }
+ }
+ > Use `accountId` in the match block — not `account`.